ice they suspected arbory  was armed and responsible for recent  burglaries in their neighborhood they're  there to detain a mod arbory for the  police this is what the law allows  the defense focused on the months  leading up to the shooting when arbory  was sometimes seen walking around a  house under construction the same  property he visited the morning of the  shooting there's no evidence arbory ever  did anything but look around the site  the accused only called 9-1-1 after they  began chasing him we think  the only right verdict is not guilty on  each and every count in this  indictment race will play a central role  in the trial there have been comparisons  to a modern day lynching  according to investigators travis  mcmichael who shot arbory allegedly used  a racial slur in the aftermath i'm very  anxious  about the trial beginning  i'm very hopeful that we'll get the  correct verdict the makeup of the jury  with only one black person has raised  concern  the defense struck 11 of 12 prospective  black jurors from the pool drawing a  rare rebuke from the judge this court  has found that there appears to be  intentional  discrimination in the panel like the  murder of george floyd in minneapolis  charges in arbory's death likely would  not have happened were it not for the  video which surfaced months later  now the accused not only face  prosecution in georgia but also a  separate trial on federal hate crime  charges  jackson prosco global news washington  still ahead the call to arms in  ethiopia's war as rebel forces advance  you're watching global national  [Music]  in mexico gunmen opened fire at a  popular resort killing two suspected  drug dealers it happened near the hyatt  ziva riviera cancun an all-inclusive  resort in puerto morelos the dramatic  attack sent tourists scrambling for  cover in the hotel police are calling it  a confrontation between rival gangs  in ethiopia the military is calling on  former soldiers to rejoin the ranks to  fight advancing rebel forces the rebels  from the northern region of tigre  announced a new alliance with other  anti-government groups they're  reportedly advancing towards the capital  but the government is digging in it's  declared a state of emergency and called  on residents to pick up arms to defend  the city this week marked one year since  the conflict erupted in that time  thousands of people have been killed  up next the push to make global trade  greener  thousands of young people marched  through glasgow today demanding more  action over their future at the cop 26  climate summit among them was  high-profile activist greta tunberg who  has accused world leaders of making  hollow commitments and pretending to  take climate change seriously speaking  at the rally she went as far to say the  summit was a failure  they are actively creating loopholes and  shaping frameworks to benefit themselves  and to continue profiting from this  destructive system a two-week long  celebration of business as usual and  blah blah blah  there is a high bar to meet the climate  challenge take ships they're huge  emission hogs but they're still vital  for trade and travel as crystal gomezing  reports a canadian company has come up  with a solution that sounds as simple as  charging your phone  measuring by volume nearly 90 percent of  world trade goods are moved on water the  international council on clean transport  says if international shipping was a  country it would be the sixth largest  emitter of greenhouse gas emissions  based on 2015 data i spent years  building vessels and seeing around the  world the impact  that we have today with pollution  brent perry is the ceo of shift power  swap stations provide fresh energy  within minutes the canadian clean energy  company won a contract to equip 20  vessels of the port of singapore with  its pay-as-you-go power swap battery  system think of the rechargeable battery  you pop onto your power tools but on a  much larger scale the project will ramp  up to 1600 vessels within the port's  infrastructure powerswap a practical  solution to reduce the impact of climate  change  and by next year shifts power swap will  also be used on boats in the uk to  transfer workers to and from a wind farm  we'll be charging them both on shore and  using the wind generators themselves to  charge the ships so these guys will be  able to go from being a heavy polluting  element on a wind farm which is a green  energy producer to now being a partner  if you want in zero emission delivery of  the whole entire ecosystem of the wind  farm that holistic chain approach is  gaining speed ahead of cop26 nine major  companies including amazon and ikea  signed a pledge to only move cargo on  ships using zero carbon fuels by 2040  but greening the entire industry may be  as challenging as freeing a stuck ship  in the suez  a patchwork of electric and cleaner  burning fuels is likely the  international maritime organization has  set 2050 as its deadline for shipping  companies to cut the amount of carbon  dioxide emitted by vessels world leaders  meeting here in scotland just steps away  from the river clyde and its rich  shipbuilding history are set to come up  with a plan that will protect global  waterways meanwhile energy and  technology companies such as shift are  also gathering sharing best practices  and hoping to get the attention of those  leaders  crystal gomanson global news  glasgow  and that is global national for this  friday i'm robin gill tonight your  canada is madeira park on the sunshine  coast in british columbia thank you to  the surgic family for sharing the photo  we know they are very loyal viewers  there are beautiful spots all over  canada so please send us your pictures  the email is viewers globalnational.com  thank you for watching and i hope to see  you back here again tomorrow have a  great night  [Music]  you
 

